1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,240
Beth has experienced weeks of deep depression.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:07,545
At another time, she needed very little sleep, talked unusually

3
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:10,340
fast and made plans that became risky.

4
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:13,760
These were sustained changes from her usual self.

5
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:17,260
Understanding that history matters when choosing treatment.

6
00:00:17,811 --> 00:00:22,551
Bipolar disorder involves distinct episodes affecting mood, energy

7
00:00:22,611 --> 00:00:26,396
and activity. It is more than ordinary changes between feeling

8
00:00:26,411 --> 00:00:31,436
happy and sad. This episode explains contributing factors, what

9
00:00:31,451 --> 00:00:36,051
is known about the biology, and why treatment depends on the phase of illness.

10
00:00:36,636 --> 00:00:40,436
This is general information for adults, not medical advice.

11
00:00:41,136 --> 00:00:44,901
Suspected mania or severe depression needs prompt professional

12
00:00:44,916 --> 00:00:48,921
assessment. Seek urgent local help if there is immediate danger

13
00:00:48,936 --> 00:00:51,336
or someone cannot stay safe.

14
00:00:51,776 --> 00:00:55,676
Do not stop or change prescribed treatment because of this video.

15
00:00:56,587 --> 00:01:00,972
During mania, mood may be unusually elevated or irritable, with

16
00:01:00,987 --> 00:01:05,732
increased energy, less need for sleep and changes in judgement.

17
00:01:05,747 --> 00:01:07,827
Some people lose touch with reality.

18
00:01:08,347 --> 00:01:11,952
The disruption can be severe enough to need hospital care, even

19
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:14,167
when the person feels exceptionally well.

20
00:01:14,644 --> 00:01:17,824
Bipolar one includes at least one manic episode.

21
00:01:18,384 --> 00:01:22,689
Bipolar two involves depression and hypomania, a less severe

22
00:01:22,704 --> 00:01:27,029
form of elevated or irritable mood and increased activity, without

23
00:01:27,044 --> 00:01:33,224
full mania. Bipolar two can still cause serious suffering, especially through depression.

24
00:01:33,768 --> 00:01:37,113
Assessment follows the person's history over time, including

25
00:01:37,128 --> 00:01:40,868
sleep, medicines, substances and physical health.

26
00:01:41,468 --> 00:01:44,688
Family observations can help, with the person's agreement.

27
00:01:45,268 --> 00:01:49,133
A single low mood, brief burst of energy or laboratory result

28
00:01:49,148 --> 00:01:51,008
does not settle the diagnosis.

29
00:01:52,076 --> 00:01:55,136
Inherited vulnerability is strongly established.

30
00:01:55,616 --> 00:01:59,541
Many genetic differences contribute, usually with small individual

31
00:01:59,556 --> 00:02:03,436
effects. Some overlap with other mental health conditions.

32
00:02:03,936 --> 00:02:08,441
These findings do not identify one bipolar gene, and family history

33
00:02:08,456 --> 00:02:10,416
does not make the illness inevitable.

34
00:02:11,072 --> 00:02:15,177
Adversity, stress and substance use can matter, but a risk factor

35
00:02:15,192 --> 00:02:17,512
is not the same as an episode trigger.

36
00:02:18,132 --> 00:02:21,332
Cannabis is associated with later bipolar symptoms;

37
00:02:21,752 --> 00:02:24,592
shared vulnerabilities complicate the causal picture.

38
00:02:25,152 --> 00:02:29,392
One event rarely provides a complete explanation for a person's illness.

39
00:02:30,004 --> 00:02:33,424
Sleep has a particularly close relationship with episodes.

40
00:02:34,004 --> 00:02:37,489
Sleep loss can contribute to an episode, be an early sign of

41
00:02:37,504 --> 00:02:41,969
one, or worsen it. Mania can itself reduce the felt need for

42
00:02:41,984 --> 00:02:45,804
sleep. The relationship can therefore run in both directions.

43
00:02:46,819 --> 00:02:50,979
Researchers study brain networks involved in emotion, reward,

44
00:02:51,239 --> 00:02:55,839
attention and control. Chemical messengers, including dopamine,

45
00:02:56,219 --> 00:03:00,144
help those networks communicate. Their involvement does not establish

46
00:03:00,159 --> 00:03:05,259
a simple rule that mania means too much of one chemical and depression too little.

47
00:03:05,751 --> 00:03:10,156
Other findings concern how cells regulate activity, supply energy

48
00:03:10,171 --> 00:03:14,671
and respond to stress. Inflammation may be relevant in some people.

49
00:03:15,091 --> 00:03:18,616
These are promising research directions, but differences measured

50
00:03:18,631 --> 00:03:24,551
during illness may reflect causes, consequences, treatment or other health conditions.

51
00:03:25,045 --> 00:03:29,170
There is no complete biological explanation for why a particular

52
00:03:29,185 --> 00:03:33,910
episode begins or ends. Nor does bipolar disorder inevitably

53
00:03:33,925 --> 00:03:36,505
cause progressive loss of thinking ability.

54
00:03:37,125 --> 00:03:40,950
Treatment can help without a complete theory: responding to lithium

55
00:03:40,965 --> 00:03:43,465
does not show that someone lacked lithium.

56
00:03:44,377 --> 00:03:47,637
The first treatment question is: what needs treating now?

57
00:03:48,097 --> 00:03:52,382
Mania, bipolar depression and prevention of future episodes require

58
00:03:52,397 --> 00:03:56,562
different choices. Medicines sometimes called mood stabilisers

59
00:03:56,577 --> 00:04:01,402
are not interchangeable. Previous benefits, side effects, other

60
00:04:01,417 --> 00:04:04,257
illnesses and the person's preferences all matter.

61
00:04:04,781 --> 00:04:08,806
For mania, effective options include certain antipsychotic medicines

62
00:04:08,821 --> 00:04:13,361
and lithium. Antipsychotic is the name of a medicine group;

63
00:04:13,621 --> 00:04:16,481
their use does not mean every person has psychosis.

64
00:04:17,301 --> 00:04:22,141
Severe episodes may need a combination and close support or hospital treatment.

65
00:04:22,689 --> 00:04:26,549
Bipolar depression needs treatment with evidence for that phase.

66
00:04:27,029 --> 00:04:31,134
Quetiapine is one established option, with other choices depending

67
00:04:31,149 --> 00:04:35,674
on circumstances. Antidepressants alone are not recommended for

68
00:04:35,689 --> 00:04:40,534
bipolar one depression. Selected use alongside appropriate bipolar

69
00:04:40,549 --> 00:04:43,829
treatment requires clinical judgement and monitoring.

70
00:04:44,352 --> 00:04:48,377
For a severe or resistant episode, a specialist may recommend

71
00:04:48,392 --> 00:04:53,557
ECT. During a brief general anaesthetic, a controlled electrical

72
00:04:53,572 --> 00:04:58,117
stimulus produces a seizure. It can be effective, but needs discussion

73
00:04:58,132 --> 00:05:01,532
of memory problems, including gaps that can persist.

74
00:05:02,575 --> 00:05:06,140
After improvement, continuing treatment can reduce the chance

75
00:05:06,155 --> 00:05:10,620
of another episode. Lithium is a leading option, particularly

76
00:05:10,635 --> 00:05:14,635
for preventing mania, and several alternatives also work.

77
00:05:15,095 --> 00:05:18,680
The best plan takes account of previous response and whether

78
00:05:18,695 --> 00:05:22,195
depressive or manic episodes have been the main difficulty.

79
00:05:22,765 --> 00:05:24,565
Monitoring is part of treatment.

80
00:05:25,065 --> 00:05:28,510
Lithium needs blood-level checks and monitoring of kidney and

81
00:05:28,525 --> 00:05:33,070
thyroid health. Dehydration and interacting medicines can increase

82
00:05:33,085 --> 00:05:36,950
toxicity risk. Other treatments may require checks for weight

83
00:05:36,965 --> 00:05:39,665
gain, sleepiness or other effects.

84
00:05:40,125 --> 00:05:42,985
Discuss pregnancy plans early with the care team.

85
00:05:43,868 --> 00:05:47,948
Structured psychological care adds benefit alongside medication.

86
00:05:48,588 --> 00:05:52,513
It can teach early warning signs, coping with stress, steadier

87
00:05:52,528 --> 00:05:56,813
routines and better communication. Family sessions can help when

88
00:05:56,828 --> 00:06:01,193
wanted. The evidence mainly concerns this care added to medication,

89
00:06:01,208 --> 00:06:03,008
rather than replacing it.

90
00:06:03,461 --> 00:06:07,446
Beth's plan includes regular sleep, people she can contact and

91
00:06:07,461 --> 00:06:09,881
an agreed response to early changes.

92
00:06:10,461 --> 00:06:14,446
Practical support with work, housing, physical health or substance

93
00:06:14,461 --> 00:06:16,381
use may also be needed.

94
00:06:16,881 --> 00:06:21,521
A plan made during a stable period can guide help when judgement becomes harder.

95
00:06:22,009 --> 00:06:24,649
Recovery is more than a lower symptom score.

96
00:06:25,029 --> 00:06:28,554
It includes relationships, meaningful activity and treatment

97
00:06:28,569 --> 00:06:33,094
that remains tolerable. Episodes can recur, but recurrence is

98
00:06:33,109 --> 00:06:34,749
a reason to review care.

99
00:06:35,189 --> 00:06:39,669
With sustained support, many people build stable and satisfying lives.
